Issues Encountered
Incorrect/missing package and folder structure initially caused Java classes to be difficult to compile and integrate.
The demonstration program initially did not contain all selected instruction types.
Incomplete multi-byte instructions were not initially detected correctly when an operand byte was missing.
SJMP instruction required careful handling of signed relative offsets and PC updates.

Decisions Made
Decided to use and implement 10 instructions.
Use HALT as a simulator-defined termination instruction.

